DTSTART:20260808T070000
DTEND:20260808T090000
SUMMARY:[AI ADJUSTED] cycling — 60–75 min Z1–low-Z2 spin at 128–145
 W\, flat route\, no distanc
DESCRIPTION:60–75 min Z1–low-Z2 spin at 128–145W\, flat route\, no di
 stance target — treat as a systems check\; only extend to 84km if body b
 attery on waking is ≥55 AND sleep averaged ≥6.5h for Aug 4–7.\n\nRea
 son: Body battery has been at or near critical levels (2–31) for the pas
 t 5 days and the last completed long ride was July 20\; a full 84km effort
  on depleted reserves risks compounding the fatigue hole rather than build
 ing aerobic fitness.\n\nAI coaching 2026-08-01
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai-coaching-20260809-2@jean-tri
DTSTAMP:20260801T092206Z
DTSTART:20260809T070000
DTEND:20260809T090000
SUMMARY:[AI ADJUSTED] running — 8km easy walk-run at 7:00–7:30/km\, HR 
 cap ≤140 bpm\, 55–65 mi
DESCRIPTION:8km easy walk-run at 7:00–7:30/km\, HR cap ≤140 bpm\, 55–
 65 min — gate: only run if Aug 8 ride was completed and morning body bat
 tery is ≥50\; otherwise a 40-min flat walk at conversational effort.\n\n
 Reason: Running volume cannot safely step up to 12km the day after a long 
 ride when the athlete is coming off near-zero sleep nights (41 min on July
  27\, 278 min on July 28) — a conservative walk-run protects against inj
 ury while re-establishing the aerobic base.\n\nAI coaching 2026-08-01
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai-coaching-20260821-3@jean-tri
DTSTAMP:20260801T092206Z
DTSTART:20260821T070000
DTEND:20260821T090000
SUMMARY:[AI ADJUSTED] swimming — 60 min pool session: 2\,500m with Half O
 ceanman-specific set 
DESCRIPTION:60 min pool session: 2\,500m with Half Oceanman-specific set 
 — 400m warm-up\, 3×600m @ 2:25/100m with 30-sec rest\, 300m cool-down\;
  begin race-simulation pacing to stress-test 2:30/100m target over longer 
 continuous efforts.\n\nReason: With the Half Oceanman 5km swim 63 days awa
 y\, Week 9 is the right inflection point to start extending continuous swi
 m sets beyond 2km and practising race pace over longer intervals to build 
 the confidence and aerobic capacity needed for 5\,000m open water.\n\nAI c
 oaching 2026-08-01
END:VEVENT
