DTSTART:20261009T070000
DTEND:20261009T090000
SUMMARY:[AI ADJUSTED] rest — Full rest day — no swimming\, no cross-tra
 ining\; optional 10-
DESCRIPTION:Full rest day — no swimming\, no cross-training\; optional 10
 -min walk and light stretching only.\n\nReason: A 60-min pool session 2 da
 ys before a 10K race adds residual muscular fatigue and risks disrupting t
 he taper — complete rest protects leg freshness and ensures peak neuromu
 scular readiness for race day.\n\nAI coaching 2026-08-01
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai-coaching-20261010-5@jean-tri
DTSTAMP:20260801T092206Z
DTSTART:20261010T070000
DTEND:20261010T090000
SUMMARY:[AI ADJUSTED] rest — Short 15-min shakeout run at 6:00–6:15/km 
 (race pace feel\, n
DESCRIPTION:Short 15-min shakeout run at 6:00–6:15/km (race pace feel\, n
 o HR pressure) + 5 min of light leg swings and hip mobility — total 20 m
 in\; no cycling at all.\n\nReason: A 4-hour long ride the day before a 10K
  race would devastate glycogen stores and leave the legs fatigued — repl
 acing with a brief race-pace shakeout activates the neuromuscular system w
 ithout accumulating fatigue.\n\nAI coaching 2026-08-01
END:VEVENT
